      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Generally, the industry standard differentiates political satire by its intent to critique or mock, whereas hate speech targets protected groups with incitement to violence or direct harassment. Satire often relies on exaggeration and hyperbole to make a point, while hate speech is rooted in hostility and dehumanization against identity characteristics. Moderators are usually trained to look for the *effect*—whether the content aims to provoke discrimination rather than just prompt laughter or debate.",
